# A lambda parameter is the type it is used at (D165).
== SOURCE
u:f_ := { x -> (x + 1.5) + (x = "a") }
== ERROR
error[type-mismatch]: expected Float, found Char
 --> -e:1:29
  |
1 | u:f_ := { x -> (x + 1.5) + (x = "a") }
  |                             ^^^^^^^
  |                             - `x`, the lambda's parameter, is a Float as it is used
  |                                 --- a string: a vector of Char
  = note: `=` has type (Eq a, Truthy b) => a -> a -> b
